Temporary Staffing Platform (A3) - INSTALL

Environment used
- Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (or equivalent Linux VM/container)
- Node.js 20+ and npm 10+
- SQLite3 via Prisma (local file database)

Important platform note
- The backend writes SQLite DB files and uploads to local disk.
- On many PaaS providers this storage is ephemeral, so data may be lost on restart/redeploy.
- This submission assumes single-user usage and does not guarantee persistence across redeployments.

Prerequisites
1) Install Node.js and npm
   - Example:
     - curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_20.x | sudo -E bash -
     - sudo apt-get install -y nodejs
2) Verify versions:
   - node -v
   - npm -v

Project structure
- backend/: Express + Prisma + SQLite API
- frontend/: React (Vite) app
- Makefile: helper clean/zip targets

Backend setup
1) Open terminal in backend:
   - cd backend
2) Install packages:
   - npm install
3) Seed database:
   - npm run seed
4) Start server:
   - npm start
5) Backend runs at:
   - http://localhost:3000

CORS (browser frontend)
- The backend enables CORS so the React app can call the API from another origin (e.g. Vite on port 5173).
- By default all origins are allowed (`origin: true`). For production, set a comma-separated allowlist:
  - export CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-frontend.example,http://localhost:5173

Frontend setup
1) Open terminal in frontend:
   - cd frontend
2) Install packages:
   - npm install
3) (Optional) Set backend API URL:
   - export VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
   - If omitted, frontend defaults to http://localhost:3000
4) Start dev server:
   - npm run dev
5) Frontend runs at:
   - http://localhost:5173

Production build (frontend)
1) Build static assets:
   - cd frontend
   - npm run build
2) Output directory:
   - frontend/dist

Simple deployment approach (single VM preferred)
Use one Ubuntu VM with both frontend and backend processes.

Backend deployment
1) Deploy repository to VM.
2) Run in backend/:
   - npm install
   - npm run seed
   - npm start
3) Keep process alive with systemd/pm2/screen.

Frontend deployment
Option A: Static hosting behind Nginx
1) Build frontend:
   - cd frontend && npm install && npm run build
2) Serve frontend/dist with Nginx.
3) Configure reverse proxy for backend API to backend process (port 3000), or set VITE_API_BASE_URL to public backend URL before build.

Option B: Same machine, separate process
1) Serve frontend assets with any static server:
   - npm install -g serve
   - cd frontend && serve -s dist -l 4173
2) Keep backend on port 3000.

Nginx notes (recommended)
- Serve frontend as SPA and rewrite unknown routes to index.html.
- Proxy API requests (for example /auth, /users, /jobs, etc.) to backend at http://127.0.0.1:3000.
- Ensure CORS/backend base URL settings align with your deployment domain.